      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day, which is twice the FDA-labeled maximum for metformin. The maximum is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release and 2,000 mg/day for extended-release. A dose that high raises the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nThe intended dose may have been one of these:\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals.** This is 2,550 mg/day, the max for immediate-release.\n- **1,700 mg total per day.** This could be 850 mg twice daily with meals.\n- **500 mg or 1,000 mg PO twice daily with meals.** These are common regimens.\n\nFor a new start, the usual approach is 500 mg once or twice daily with meals, then titrating up every 1\u20132 weeks as tolerated.\n\nPlease confirm the dose and frequency you want, and check with your resident or attending. I'll enter the order as soon as you confirm. If you do want the original dose, tell me the clinical reason and I'll enter it with a note for pharmacist review."
      }
     ],
